 ],
 "scope_and_limitations": "Confirmed from source construction paths in the supplied non-Git source snapshot. No files were changed, and no network requests or runtime probes were run. The helper comment says ChatGPT groups caching by session-id and ignores body prompt_cache_key (src/orchestration/agent-runtime/llm/openai-helpers.ts:246-251), but actual remote backend cache behavior is not verified here. The report establishes what this code constructs and dispatches, not whether a provider records a cache hit."
}

{
 "summary": "Confirmed: the hosted Claude route waits for the engine's signed-thinking row after its stop chunk, polling every 20 ms for up to 10 seconds. The delay ends as soon as the row appears, or on timeout with a transient stream error. Aborting the request marks the hosted agent gone; the next request plans a fresh dispatch and creates a new agent id, not a resume of that agent. The new dispatch writes the then-current hosted conversation view; these paths do not establish whether the stopped partial response is present in that canonical view.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "claim": "The signature wait has a 10-second bound after the step's stop chunk. It polls the agent file every 20 ms; the missing signed-block row ends the wait by either appearing or by raising a transient stream error after the bound.",
   "evidence": [
