{
 "summary": "A person-facing chat waits until the route's stated capacity reset, then continues the chat automatically; an unattended chat does not wait for a spent usage limit, even when its reset was stated. It can still wait when another route has an independently self-clearing hold, until that hold's reset/recheck time. Neither path applies backoff to the spent-quota failure itself; the shared provider walk does use bounded backoff for other retryable failures.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  "Person-facing chat: `createChatCapacityWait` passes `unattendedRun: input.unattended` into the common recovery policy (`src/orchestration/chat/chat-capacity-wait.ts:14-28`). For a chat API error with recovery kind `at`, recovery enters `capacityWait` (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/unattended-recovery.ts:313-318`). In non-unattended mode, a usage-limit hold uses the recovery's stated reset; the wait targets `atMs` with wall-clock timing, then recovery returns `{}` to continue (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/unattended-recovery.ts:274-301`). The wait records/show notices, and ends at that reset or earlier if interrupted/a person sends a message (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/unattended-recovery.ts:206-239`, `src/orchestration/agent-runtime/unattended-recovery.ts:342-347`).",
  "Unattended chat: for `unattendedRun === true` and `usage_limit`, policy substitutes `recovery.selfClearing`; if absent, it records failure and returns `null` immediately, rather than waiting for the stated usage-limit reset (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/unattended-recovery.ts:274-279`). It waits if `selfClearing` exists, through its `atMs`, then continues (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/unattended-recovery.ts:280-301`). `selfClearing` is the earliest reset among other candidate holds that are not usage limits; the recovery builder returns it only when the earliest overall hold is a usage limit (`src/infra/llm/provider-error-copy.ts:121-138`). Thus an unattended run can wait when another route has an independently clearing rate-limit/recheck hold, for the remaining time until that hold's `atMs`, not for a fixed usage-limit delay. The source describes those hold kinds and their meanings at `src/infra/llm/provider-error-copy.ts:89-96`.",
  "Backoff: not for quota exhaustion. The shared failover loop handles `QuotaExhaustedFailure` and breaks before the retry branch (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/llm/failover-client.ts:646-655`); it then advances the candidate walk (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/llm/failover-client.ts:674-675`). For other retryable route failures, it allows three in-place retries (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/llm/failover-client.ts:122-130`, `src/orchestration/agent-runtime/llm/failover-client.ts:657-665`) with provider-declared delay capped at 60 seconds or exponential jittered backoff (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/llm/failover-client.ts:140-147`). Separately, unattended recovery's `freshAttempt` applies exponential pauses starting at 5 seconds for eligible non-quota failures (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/unattended-recovery.ts:68-75`, `src/orchestration/agent-runtime/unattended-recovery.ts:242-265`); a chat's usage-limit path instead goes through `capacityWait` (`src/orchestration/agent-runtime/unattended-recovery.ts:313-318`)."
 ]
}

